# rule.always.boot-an-oversized-subdomain-as-its-catalog

when an enbriefed subdomain is too large to boot whole, boot its catalog at `say` and list every member under `not`. each member stays reffable via a path the catalog lets a reader compute.

```yaml
say:
  - briefs/domain.terms/catalog.of=term._.md     # every name + the path formula
not:
  - briefs/domain.terms/term=*.md                # members: read on demand
```

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a boot spec globs ~20+ files of one subdomain | catalog it |
| `rhx cost` ranks `<briefs.ref>` / `<also>` near the top | the path list is the cost |
| a boot spec runs over budget | cut paths before cues |
| a subdomain begins to fill a directory | write its catalog at the second member |
| members are named by coordinate | state the path formula once |

the catalog owes: every member by name grouped by boundary root · the path formula with an example · a census note · its rules by path. it obeys `rule.require.catalog-is-an-index`.

blocker: catalog at `say` whose members are left out of `not`.
nitpick: catalogable subdomain of ~20+ members booted as paths · catalog that prints every path where one formula computes it.
false positive: a handful of files at ref · subdomain every boot needs whole.

⇒ `rule.require.catalog-is-an-index` · `rule.prefer.rules-that-refout`
